{
  "__comment": "Which days a calendar event covers and how a multi-day one is spelled — the ONE set of cases both sides are tested against: the SPA (client/src/utils/calendar.ts eventDaySpan + calendarViews.ts spanDays, test client/src/utils/calendarSpanCases.test.ts) and the household dashboard (socialhome/domain/calendar.py event_day_span + socialhome/dashboard/clock.py span_label, test tests/domain/test_calendar_span_cases.py). Timed events are read in the viewer's zone, which is UTC for every case here (the vitest run and viewer_tz). label_en is null for a one-day event.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "timed three days",
      "start": "2026-05-01T14:00:00Z", "end": "2026-05-03T10:00:00Z", "all_day": false, "tz": null,
      "first": "2026-05-01", "last": "2026-05-03", "day_count": 3,
      "label_en": "Fri 1 – Sun 3 · 3 days"
    },
    {
